{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Logic gates",
  "exampleId": "block-logic-gates",
  "description": "A is true for the first half of every second, B for the first second of every two. Read the gates at 0.25 s (A and B true), 0.75 s (only B), and 1.75 s (neither): AND is true only at 0.25 s, OR at 0.25 and 0.75 s, XOR only at 0.75 s, NAND and NOR are their inverses, and NOT inverts A. Boolean to real turns the NOT output into 0 or 1 for arithmetic.",
